---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Comments from "../../components/Comments.astro";
import { whatsappLink } from "../../config";
---

<Layout
	title="WhatsApp Business Kenya: Setup Tutorial (Copy-Paste) | Orbit"
	description="Turn WhatsApp into sales: Business profile, catalog, quick replies, labels and click-to-chat — copy-paste setup, free DIY."
>
	<Navbar />
	<main id="main">
		<section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-white/5">
			<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true">
				<div class="absolute -top-40 left-1/3 h-[400px] w-[600px] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-electric/15 blur-[130px]"></div>
			</div>
			<div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-14 pt-20 md:pt-28">
				<p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-electric">■ Guides · WhatsApp · 5 min</p>
				<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
					Turn WhatsApp into <span class="text-gradient">your best salesperson.</span>
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-5 text-lg text-slate-400">Free setup you can do this afternoon — templates to copy.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">WhatsApp is where Kenyan buyers live — 97% of smartphone users have it. But most small businesses use personal WhatsApp, missing the profile, catalog and automation tools that turn casual chats into sales. This guide sets up Business in one afternoon, free.</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-white">1) Business profile (5 min)</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> Download WhatsApp Business (separate from regular WhatsApp — same number works).</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> Profile photo = your logo. Cover photo = your best product or shopfront. People judge trust in 2 seconds.</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> Business name: exact brand name, not a tagline. Category: pick the most specific one (e.g. "Clothing shop" not "Clothing store").</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> Description: what you sell + where + delivery. Example: "Handmade leather bags in Nairobi CBD. Delivery countrywide via Fargo. M-Pesa & cards."</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> Address: use Google Maps pin, not just "Nairobi". Hours: exact, including lunch break if you close. Empty profile = no trust.</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> Catalog: add top 10 products with photos, names, prices, short descriptions. This is your shop window — treat it like a physical display.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-white">2) Greeting + away messages</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Settings → Business Tools → Greeting/Away. These auto-reply when someone messages you for the first time or after hours.</p>
			<div class="mt-4 rounded-xl bg-panel border border-edge p-5 text-sm text-slate-300">
				<p class="font-mono text-xs text-electric font-semibold">Greeting message</p>
				<p class="mt-2">Hi! Thanks for reaching [Biz]. We reply in minutes, 8am–7pm daily. Tell me what you need — price, size, delivery? I'll sort you fast.</p>
				<p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-electric font-semibold">Away message</p>
				<p class="mt-2">Hey! We're offline 7pm–8am but your message is saved — first thing at 8am. For urgent orders, call [phone]. Asante!</p>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Tip: greeting fires once per contact, not every message. Away fires only during your set off-hours.</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-white">3) Quick replies + labels</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Settings → Business Tools → Quick Replies. Set up shortcuts for your most common answers — saves 5+ min per enquiry:</p>
			<div class="mt-4 grid gap-2 font-mono text-xs">
				<div class="rounded-lg border border-edge bg-panel p-4 text-slate-300"><span class="text-electric font-semibold">/price</span> — It's KES [price] + delivery [fee]. M-Pesa Paybill [number] Account [your phone]. Want an invoice?</div>
				<div class="rounded-lg border border-edge bg-panel p-4 text-slate-300"><span class="text-electric font-semibold">/location</span> — We're at [exact address], open [hours]. Pin: [Google Maps link]. Parking available.</div>
				<div class="rounded-lg border border-edge bg-panel p-4 text-slate-300"><span class="text-electric font-semibold">/delivery</span> — Nairobi same-day KES [X]. Upcountry 1–3 days via Fargo/G4S. Pickup free at [location].</div>
				<div class="rounded-lg border border-edge bg-panel p-4 text-slate-300"><span class="text-electric font-semibold">/hours</span> — Mon–Sat 8am–7pm, Sunday 10am–4pm. Public holidays 10am–2pm.</div>
				<div class="rounded-lg border border-edge bg-panel p-4 text-slate-300"><span class="text-electric font-semibold">/mpesa</span> — Paybill 123456, Account [phone]. Or Till 12345 at shop. Send screenshot to confirm.</div>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-400">Labels: <span class="text-white font-semibold">New</span> · <span class="text-white font-semibold">Quoted</span> · <span class="text-white font-semibold">Paid</span> · <span class="text-white font-semibold">Shipped</span> · <span class="text-white font-semibold">VIP</span> — label every chat, filter daily, never lose a lead. Move "New" → "Quoted" after replying, → "Paid" after M-Pesa screenshot, → "Shipped" after dispatch.</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-white">4) Click-to-chat links</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">A click-to-chat link opens a WhatsApp chat with your number and a pre-filled message. Put it on your website, Instagram bio, Google Business Profile, flyers, and receipts. Pattern:</p>
			<div class="mt-4 rounded-xl bg-panel border border-edge p-4 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300">https://wa.me/2547XXXXXXXX?text=Hi!%20I%20want%20[product]%20size%20[colour]%20delivered%20to%20[estate]</div>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Why pre-filled? It removes the "what do I say?" friction. Messages with context convert 3x higher than "Hi". Put YOUR number (with country code, no + or spaces) and a message that matches what the person is likely looking for.</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-white">5) Broadcast lists vs groups</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Use broadcast lists, not groups. Broadcasts send to each person individually (they don't see other recipients), and replies come to you privately. Groups create noise and lose messages. Create lists by segment: "New customers", "VIPs", "Nairobi", "Mombasa". Send max 2x/week — daily broadcasts get blocked.</p>

			<div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-edge bg-panel p-6">
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Where Orbit fits</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">DIY above in an afternoon, or WhatsApp Responder 35,999: we do profile + catalog + labels + quick replies + site buttons + click-to-chat in one go. <a href={whatsappLink("Hi Orbit! Set up my WhatsApp Business properly.")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-electric hover:underline">Set mine up →</a></p>
			</div>
		</article>

		<Comments slug="whatsapp-business-kenya" />
		<CtaBand title="Your customers are already chatting." text="Be the business that answers first — in minutes, Mon–Sat." />
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
